  "verificationScope": "# Original Koszul cut: actual local ring Ext and affine coefficient restriction\n\nLet R be ANY commutative ring,r=n+1>=1,H=(H_1,...,H_r) the ORIGINAL\nordered list,and I=(H). Let K_j be the ACTUAL exterior-power Koszul\nmodules of R^r,and v_r the ORIGINAL ordered top generator. Then\n image(DUAL ORIGINAL TOP DIFFERENTIAL) maps to EXACTLY I,\n coker(d_r^*) ~= R/I,[L] -> L(v_r) modulo ORIGINAL I.\nAll complementary determinant signs are PROVED,not assumed.\n\nLet in addition ORIGINAL List.ofFn H be REGULAR. Use the EXISTING ACTUAL\noriginal functionKoszulResolution and mathlib ProjectiveResolution.extMk.\nThen a REAL DERIVED R-MODULE EXT equivalence is CONSTRUCTED:\n Ext_R^r(R/I,R) ~=_R R/I,\n [top functional L] -> L(v_r) modulo I.\nLet eps_R be the ACTUAL Ext class represented by ORIGINAL top coordinate.\nFor ANY ORIGINAL R-linear a:R->R,push along a goes to a(1) modulo I.\nIn particular,multiplication by a coefficient gives that coefficient\nrestricted to ORIGINAL Spec(R/I). Every actual Ext class has a top\nrepresentative;zero iff original coefficient in I. No Ext/model,\ncomparison,push or desired cokernel premise is added.\n\nThe ACTUAL affine associated-sheaf dual-top presentation on Spec(R)\nends in the ACTUAL ORIGINAL closed-cut structure sheaf pushed forward:\n ~Dual_R(K_(r-1)) -> ~Dual_R(K_r) -> i_*O_(Spec(R/I)) ->0.\nIts exactness and epi are DERIVED using proved actual tilde exactness\nand ORIGINAL quotient pushforward iso. No regularity is needed here.\n\nLet R be ANY commutative ring,r=n+1,H the ORIGINAL ordered Fin(r) list. Actual ORIGINAL complementary determinant signs and actual dual-top image ideal are PROVED. Actual dual-top cokernel sends [L] to ORIGINAL L(top generator) modulo ORIGINAL (H),no regularity needed. For ORIGINAL REGULAR H,the EXISTING ACTUAL functionKoszulResolution is used with pinned mathlib ProjectiveResolution.extMk and actual ModuleCat HasExt:every real derived R-module Ext^r class has an ORIGINAL top functional representative,zero iff its original coefficient belongs to (H),and push along ORIGINAL R-linear a preserves representative a o L. A CONSTRUCTED R-linear ACTUAL Ext^r_R(R/(H),R) equivalence with ORIGINAL R/(H) sends representative to ORIGINAL coefficient;push of ACTUAL ordered top-coordinate Ext class goes to a(1) modulo(H). No Ext/comparison model,desired push/naturality/cokernel or regularity substitute supplied. The ACTUAL affine associated-sheaf dual-top presentation is exact and epi onto ORIGINAL closed-cut structure sheaf pushed forward along SAME original quotient map. This uses actual tilde exactness already proved;it is not yet the internal-sheaf-Hom/gluing identification. Global ORIGINAL sigma_1,...,sigma_r sheaf extension epsilon and its connecting class,global a_*epsilon=a|_S,derived SHEAF/proper-duality and uniform fixed-m remain OPEN. Normalized theta UNVERIFIED;original4.1/4.2/main OPEN,checkpoint180. Onecompiler/8GiB/2threads/CPU25%/20min unchanged.\n\nOPEN: actual internal-sheaf-Hom identification,ORIGINAL local-frame\nrestrictions/gluing,ORIGINAL GLOBAL Koszul extension eps and connecting\nclass,global a_*eps=a|_S,derived SHEAF/proper-duality,uniform fixed-m\nsections. Normalized theta UNVERIFIED;ORIGINAL4.1/4.2/main OPEN,\ncheckpoint180. Fixed m BEFORE ALL original Setup/iterates. The actual\nring Ext result is NOT called global sheaf Ext or the main theorem.\n\n5 root modules,429 physical root lines,27 exact roots\n(17 proofs,10 definitions).\n24 closed modules,19 byte-identical\nolder frozen dependencies. Full types read;transitive axioms only\npropext,Classical.choice,Quot.sound. Every actual compiler/audit through\nlean_runner.run_file,onecompiler,8GiB WindowsJob,2threads,CPU<=25%,\n20minute timeout,alloldholds retained. Ordinary elaboration errors\ncorrected;failed source not counted. Limits unchanged,no whole-project\nor remote Lean CI claim. Lean4.35.0-rc3,\nmathlib2a885768dae569d938bb9ff3474da6a8753bb90a.\nOriginal manuscript PDF SHA256:\n503864b699ae2b315ff857a57f33fb1d722ab53f331040ae6afafcd2e691ef2a.\nCompile closed sources in dependency order with same guard then\nCheckAxioms.lean;reviewed original Apache2.0 source attribution retained.\n",
  "remainingObligations": [
